This patch only adds BOOT_DEVICE_CPGMAC to the enum in
arch/riscv/include/asm/spl.h:

  enum {
          ...
          BOOT_DEVICE_SMH,
+         BOOT_DEVICE_CPGMAC,
          BOOT_DEVICE_NONE
  };

but doesn't appear to include any code that maps a RISC-V SPL boot-source
register value to BOOT_DEVICE_CPGMAC (e.g. in a board/SoC's
spl_boot_device() implementation), nor any Kconfig/SPL_NET wiring. Is the
rest of the net-boot support already present generically in common SPL code
(net.c's spl_net_load_image() etc.) and this is genuinely the only missing
piece to let a RISC-V SPL fall through to net boot, or is there a
board-specific spl_boot_device() patch that should accompany this one so
BOOT_DEVICE_CPGMAC is actually ever returned/consumed on RISC-V?

Also, BOOT_DEVICE_CPGMAC is named after the CPGMAC peripheral used on some
non-RISC-V SoCs (e.g. OMAP/AM335x) - was this deliberately reusing the
existing shared enum value with that semantic (bootrom indicates "boot from
on-chip Ethernet MAC" generically), or should this use a more RISC-V/board-
neutral name like BOOT_DEVICE_ETH if one doesn't already exist elsewhere in
the shared enum?
